I thank you all so much for being here  with us this morning as you all know  Georgia is the state that values life we  protect the innocent  we champion the vulnerable we stand up  and speak for those unable to speak for  themselves  the life act is very simple but also  very powerful a declaration that all  life has value that all life matters and  that all life is worthy of protection I  understand like the others have said  that some oppose this legislation I  realize that some may challenge it in  the court of law but our job is to do  what is right not what is easy we are  called to be strong and courageous and  we will not back down we will always  continue to fight for life I'm signing  HB 481 this morning to ensure that all  Georgians have the opportunity to live  grow learn and prosper in our great  state through the life act we will allow  precious babies to grow up and realize  their full god-given potential  I want to thank Speaker Ralston  lieutenant governor Duncan for their  strong leadership at this state capitol  and on this issue  I like others before me stand here to  applaud representative ed Setzer and  Senator Renee Unterman  for a job well done crafting this piece  of legislation and champion this noble  cause I want to also thank my floor  leaders representative Terry Rogers Jody  lot Burt Reeves Dominic LaRue kia  senators blake Tillery and brian  Strickland for their hard work in  helping secure passage of the life fact  and finally I want to thank those behind  me into the side of those in front of me  those outside of these doors and  throughout Georgia who refused to be  silent on this issue who rejected the  status quo who believe as I do that  every baby has a right to life but  remember today is just the beginning  folks we have too many children that are  stuck in foster care the adoptions  process while we've made great strides  in Georgia we have more to do because  it's still too expensive and too  cumbersome for Georgia families the  elderly are being exploited and abused  in communities throughout our state and  our nation in countless victims of human  trafficking remain in the shadows they  deserve justice that is why we must all  continue to fight we must protect life  at all stages we must weep we must  remember our higher calling and we must  remember to work in the days months and  years ahead as we have done this year  thank you all and God bless you  I'm looking forward to signing the House  bill 481 the life that  [Applause]  [Applause]
 

